Flask-Migrate / Alembic — MCbN XP Tracker

## Schema change workflow

For any change to a model in app/db.py:

1. Make the model change.
2. Generate a migration:
   cd apps/web
   FLASK_APP=app:create_app flask db migrate -m "describe the change"
3. Review the generated file in migrations/versions/.
4. Apply locally:
   FLASK_APP=app:create_app flask db upgrade
5. Commit the migration file with your code change.

## Production (Turso/libsql)

db.create_all() runs on startup and is safe for new installs. For
existing production databases, schema changes must be applied manually
via the Turso CLI or migration scripts until libsql supports Alembic
directly. Document any manual steps in the release notes.

## Baseline

The revision a976d7d0510b is an empty baseline adopted when Flask-Migrate
was initialised (2026-03-14). All tables at that point were managed by
db.create_all(). Stamp an existing dev DB with:

   FLASK_APP=app:create_app flask db stamp head

## migrate_csv_to_sheets.py

Legacy one-time data migration script (pre-Turso). Not part of the
Alembic version history.
